1. Scope and acceptance

These terms apply to the OrgSDK material made available under this license,
including modifications of that material (the Software). The Licensor is each
copyright holder offering their material under these terms. Exercising a right
granted here means accepting these terms. Rights not expressly granted remain
with their holders.

Separately identified third-party material is governed by its own license. These
terms do not replace or restrict rights granted by third-party licenses. Retain
the applicable notices, including those accompanying dependencies and copied
source. These terms do not give ownership of your data, actions or outputs to
the Licensor.

2. Source access and sharing

You may inspect, copy and modify the Software, and share original or modified
copies without charging for the copies. Every shared copy must include these
terms and retain applicable copyright, attribution and license notices.
Identify your modifications. Recipients obtain their rights directly under
these terms and must independently qualify for running the Software. You may
not offer broader rights to the covered material than you have received.

3. Permitted operation without a separate agreement

You may run original or modified copies of the Software without a license fee:

(a) as an individual for your own personal, non-business activities; or
(b) for a business's own internal activities while its entire Organization
    Group has fewer than 15 Staff.

Business activity performed by an individual on behalf of an organization is
subject to (b), including use through a personal account or personal computer.
The threshold is 0 through 14 Staff across the Organization Group, rather than
the number of users, accounts, projects, installations or concurrent sessions.
Part-time and full-time Staff each count as one person, counted only once.

An Organization Group is a business, sole trader or other business entity
together with all entities that control it, that it controls, or that are under
common control. Control means the ability to direct an entity's management,
whether through ownership, agreement or another arrangement.

Staff are working owners, employees, and individual contractors or agency
workers regularly working in the Organization Group's operations. Inactive
investors and suppliers merely providing goods or occasional services are not
Staff. Count Staff across the whole group, including people who do not use the
Software. Dividing an operation between entities, installations or accounts
does not reduce its Staff count.

An Organization Group with 15 or more Staff must obtain a separate written
commercial license before starting or continuing to run the Software. A group
that grows to that size must obtain that permission or stop running it.

4. Hosting, resale and customer access

Regardless of Staff count, a separate written commercial license from the
relevant Licensor is required to:

(a) sell, rent, sublicense for a fee, or charge for copies of the Software;
(b) operate or host the Software for third parties as a service; or
(c) give customers or other third parties access to the Software's project,
    action-authoring, execution, orchestration or management capabilities as
    part of a product or service, including an embedded or white-label product.

These restrictions apply to direct access and to access through another user
interface, API, MCP endpoint, agent or intermediary. They apply when access is
free, charged separately, or bundled into another product or service. Renaming,
modifying or concealing the Software does not remove these restrictions.

A qualifying business may use the Software internally to carry out its own
work and deliver ordinary results to customers. Giving a customer a report or
other completed result does not by itself provide access to the Software.
Giving customers the ability to define, configure, submit or manage their own
work through the Software is access requiring a commercial license.

You may charge for consulting, installation, training, maintenance or custom
development for a qualifying recipient's own internal installation. The
recipient must control that installation, independently qualify under section
3 or hold a commercial license, and retain control of its data and accounts.
Operation solely to install, develop or maintain that recipient-controlled
installation is assessed using the recipient's eligibility, rather than the
service provider's Staff count.
This permission does not include operating a hosted service for the recipient
or licensing use on behalf of an otherwise ineligible organization.

For permission beyond these terms, contact the maintainers through the OrgSDK
organization at https://github.com/OrgSDK. A separate written agreement may
grant additional rights to material its parties are authorized to license.

5. Patents and branding

Each Licensor grants permission under patent claims it controls that would
necessarily be infringed by the unmodified Software, solely for activities
permitted by these terms. This does not cover infringement introduced by your
changes or combinations. If you bring a patent claim alleging that the
Software infringes a patent, your patent permission under this section ends.

No trademark or branding rights are granted, other than displaying the notices
required by these terms and accurately identifying the origin of the Software.
Do not imply endorsement of your modifications or services.

6. Ending and restoring permission

Permission ends automatically when you breach these terms. If you correct the
breach within 30 days after first receiving written notice of it, permission
is restored. A later breach after such restoration requires written permission
from the relevant Licensor to restore your rights. Rights of recipients who
continue to comply with these terms are unaffected by your breach.

